Troubleshooting Tips
Common Issues and Solutions
Issue 1: Nmap permission denied errors

Solution: Run commands with sudo when scanning requires root privileges
Issue 2: Python libraries not found

Solution: Ensure you're using the correct Python version and pip:
python3 --version
pip3 --version
Issue 3: Elasticsearch connection refused

Solution: Check if Elasticsearch is running:
sudo systemctl status elasticsearch
sudo journalctl -u elasticsearch
Issue 4: Kibana not accessible

Solution: Verify Kibana configuration:
sudo nano /etc/kibana/kibana.yml
Ensure server.host is set to "0.0.0.0" or "localhost"

Issue 5: No vulnerabilities found

Solution: Update Nmap script database and try different targets:
sudo nmap --script-updatedb
Performance Optimization
For Large Networks:

Use parallel scanning: nmap -T4 or nmap -T5
Limit port ranges: --top-ports 100
Use host discovery first: nmap -sn before port scanning
For Better Results:

Run scans during off-peak hours
Use different scan techniques for different services
Combine multiple scanning tools for comprehensive coverage
